<title>USA: Paper May Brent slides in late U.S. trading.</title>
<headline>Paper May Brent slides in late U.S. trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent slid in late U.S. trading on Friday, with a European company doing most of the selling and a major broker attributed with most of the buying, traders said.</p>
<p>May Brent partials traded at $20.08, $20.10, $20.12 and $20.17 a barrel, down from the IPE settlement of $20.27 a barrel.</p>
<p>April/May spreads moved at 25, 27 and 30 cents a barrel, up from 20 cents at the London close.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
